 parentChainT: a member's parent is its enclosing field (Tony, 2026-11-05, R1, R2, R3; docs/parseLabelParent.md (retired 2026-11-11, git c3180398)).
 The question each row asks is H13's "is this the same FIELD", so it reads the field column: the stale twin shares its body with the right field, and only the field column tells them apart.
 Field numbers are first-seen in the run, so pop.sh compares the walk up to the walk down, tag and number together. A row that names a tag cannot pass by a shallow walk.
 Born red on trunk: UP 1 is the stale evDeep, UP 2 MemberS, UP 3 DefinE, UP 4 MemberS. The depth-1 control is right on both builds.
 The twice-placed rows pin today; their intended value is not ruled.
